sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-planitibia-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-planitibia-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-planitibia-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila planitibia detail-tier Turing wavelength (5.13 µm, Holocene 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 75.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 overall is the pre-correction rating. The Schnakenberg PDE rendered a 12-frame 800×600 GIF whose specimen CV similarity was already 87.6, but the dispersion self-test returned Pearson r = -0.125 because activator-only initial data mixed a complex long-wave pair into the log-slope. The diffusion-ratio sweep asserted the wrong monotonicity, and the specimen radial peak locked onto the vignette at 180 µm instead of the spiral-band ridge. Those three failures are the remediation list. Dataset SHA-256 pins, the 0 Ma chronoseries statement, and the Lean statements were already in place. Overall 75.8/100 (faithfulness 72.1, reproducibility 84.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 614364984b077999780547c54c33040355b80944; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 72, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 64, Morphometric validation 68, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_planitibia_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-planitibia-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 614364984b077999780547c54c33040355b80944, image/png, 568974 B, 1632×1008 px, artifact_sha256 9d34dea3222423fbb6c33b054a6edaf242dd18b0fe1f84cac7cacccaa7359c93 (sha256 9d34dea3222423fbb6c33b054a6edaf242dd18b0fe1f84cac7cacccaa7359c93), spec_fingerprint ae50fdfd76557b94257607e992d8d85891de9e571d0334c02e62f7bd23852ae1. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: ae50fdfd76557b94257607e992d8d85891de9e571d0334c02e62f7bd23852ae1; artifact_sha256: 9d34dea3222423fbb6c33b054a6edaf242dd18b0fe1f84cac7cacccaa7359c93; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_planitibia_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=5bb5fa3afb09444b..., datasets/drosophila_planitibia_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_planitibia_specimen.jpg=4e1280925b1e63af..., datasets/drosophila_planitibia_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_planitibia_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=5fa45424d1e6731e..., datasets/drosophila_planitibia_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=7e60555a08d73b71..., datasets/drosophila_planitibia_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=0045b52532f7ea49...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation for a two-species reaction-diffusion system, and Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics a - u + u^2 v, b - u^2 v. | Edwards et al. (2007) Hawaiian Drosophila wing-diversity database and Kambysellis et al. (1995, Current Biology) picture-wing phylogeny. Neither paper reports a 5.13 µm wavelength. | Carson (1982) radiation of Drosophila on the newer Hawaiian volcanoes, the biogeographic setting of Maui D. planitibia. Geological age in this chronoseries is 0 Ma.; reconstructed_in_script: Periodic Schnakenberg integration scaled so the fastest discrete mode is the assigned detail-tier length 5.13e-06 m. | Chronoseries contrast with D. persimilis at 117 µm and D. pseudoobscura at 114 µm at fixed kinetics: activator diffusivity scales as lambda squared. Age delta is 0 Ma.; transfer_boundary: Generic Schnakenberg pigment kinetics are not a measured yellow/ebony network for D. planitibia. The 5.13 µm length is the assigned tier, not a published morphometric.; does_not_claim: That the vendored micrograph's spiral carrier equals 5.13 µm, or that DOI 10.1073/pnas.92.17.7819 is the Kambysellis phylogeny (it is a different 1995 paper). | A measured spacing of foretarsal cilia.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Measure the specimen spiral-band ridge above the vignette bins of the radial FFT. Pass 1 reported the envelope at 180 µm from a 111 px / 100 µm scale bar.",
            "remediation needed: Re-run image fitness, measure_outputs, and the knowledge-graph build on the corrected probe.",
            "remediation needed: Reseed each Turing-band Fourier mode on its leading real eigenvector, drop the complex long-wave pair, and require Pearson r > 0.98 against the discrete dispersion symbol. Pass 1 measured r = -0.125.",
            "remediation needed: Restrict the diffusion-ratio sweep to ratios with sigma_max > 0 and test the direction the fastest mode actually moves. Pass 1 asserted a decreasing lambda and the assertion failed." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.758"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (primary assessor, loop 3199 pass 1)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

